# Frontend ESLint gate (hard requirement)

This repo copies custom rules from `tilemap/eslint-rules` into `eslint-rules/`.

Configured in root `eslint.config.js`. Enforced by Cursor stop hook
`.cursor/hooks/eslint-frontend-on-stop.sh` (`eslint` + `tsc --noEmit`) and
`npm run quality`.

## Local rules (error — do not disable)

| Rule | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `local/no-magic-string` | Runtime string literals → `SCREAMING` consts, `enums.ts` / `constants/`, or allowed `*-wire.ts` / `*-schema.ts` files (`allowJsx: true` for JSX labels/classes) |
| `local/max-lines-strict` | Hard file length cap (see `scripts/code-metrics-limits.cjs`) — split modules |
| `local/complexity-strict` | Hard cyclomatic complexity cap — extract helpers |
| `local/no-repeated-array-filter` | Do not filter the same array twice; partition in one pass |

## Also error

- `@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any`
- `@typescript-eslint/consistent-type-assertions` with `assertionStyle: 'never'` (`as const` only)

## Forbidden

- `eslint-disable` for `local/*` rules
- Weakening thresholds in `scripts/code-metrics-limits.cjs` without an explicit user request

## Before declaring frontend work done

```bash
npm install   # repo root
npm run lint
npm run typecheck   # frontend tsc --noEmit — mandatory
npm run quality     # lint + typecheck + backend unit tests
```

Do not hand over with failing TypeScript. IDE red squiggles on context types
usually mean `ChatSession` / `SessionState` drifted — fix types,
then prove with `npm run typecheck`.
